1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,780
The year is 2015 A.D.

37
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:59,000
As of 12:30 PM today, a special state
of emergency has been declared

38
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,460
for the Kanto and Chubu regions
surrounding the Tokai district.

39
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:07,770
All residents must evacuate to their
designated shelters immediately.

40
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:12,510
Repeating: As of 12:30 PM today,

41
00:02:11,650 --> 00:02:14,070
All Lines Stopped

42
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:16,330
the Kanto and Chubu regions
surrounding the Tokai district

43
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:19,300
have been declared to be under
a state of emergency.

44
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,750
All residents must evacuate...

45
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:24,190
Why did I have to lose sight of him now?

46
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:26,120
Oh, man!

47
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,750
Shinji Ikari

48
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,840
Due to the special emergency,

49
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,500
all lines are currently unavailable.

50
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:35,300
It's no use.

51
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:39,050
I shouldn't have come here after all.

52
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:45,260
To Shinji
I'll be coming to get you,
so wait for me.
Attention here please!!

53
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:45,260
Well, I guess we won't be meeting here.

54
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:49,230
Can't be helped. I'll go to a shelter.

55
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,550
Estimated Path

56
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,550
The unidentified mobile object is still
advancing on our position.

57
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:22,430
We've got visual confirmation.
I'm putting it on the main screen.

58
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:25,730
It's been fifteen years, hasn't it?

59
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:27,840
Yes, there's no doubt.

60
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:30,480
It's an Angel.

61
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:33,190
EPISODE ONE
ANGEL ATTACK

62
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,170
Every missile hit the target!

63
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:04,890
I'm sorry! Thanks for waiting!

64
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:26,480
The target is still operational.
It's still heading towards New Tokyo-3.

65
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:29,370
The Air Defense Force doesn't have
the firepower to stop it!

66
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,110
Hit it with everything we've got!

67
00:04:31,110 --> 00:04:33,150
Mobilize all of Atsugi and Iruma as well!

68
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:36,330
Don't hold anything back!
Destroy the target at any cost!

69
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:52,430
Why?! That was a direct hit!

70
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:54,340
The tank battalion's been annihilated.

71
00:04:54,850 --> 00:04:57,890
Guided missiles and artillery
have no effect either.

72
00:04:57,890 --> 00:05:01,110
It's no good! We'll never get anywhere
with the firepower we've got!

73
00:05:01,110 --> 00:05:03,320
Is it an AT field after all?

74
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,860
Yes. Conventional weapons are
useless against Angels.

75
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:13,500
I understand. We'll activate it as planned.

76
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,050
Hey, don't tell me...

77
00:05:20,050 --> 00:05:21,750
They're going to use an N2 mine?!

78
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:23,630
Get down!

79
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:46,990
We did it!

80
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,530
Sorry, but it looks like you won't be
getting a shot at it.

81
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,860
Shock wave approaching.

82
00:05:55,010 --> 00:05:56,520
Are you all right?

83
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:59,940
Yeah, but my mouth is full of dirt.

84
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:04,090
That's okay. Now then, here we go!

85
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:06,180
One, two!

86
00:06:13,010 --> 00:06:14,130
There.

87
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:16,740
Thanks for the hand. I really appreciate it.

88
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:19,880
Thank you too, Miss Katsuragi.

89
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,840
Just Misato is fine.

90
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:26,060
I'm glad we've met at last, Shinji Ikari.

91
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,190
Yeah...

92
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,870
What's the target's status?

93
00:06:28,870 --> 00:06:31,320
We're unable to confirm due to
all the EMP interference.

94
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:34,240
You saw the size of the explosion. It's over.

95
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,240
Sensors restored.

96
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:39,080
We've got an energy reading
at the explosion's epicenter!

97
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,080
What the hell?!

98
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,230
Visual display restored.

99
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:48,310
That was our last resort.

100
00:06:49,350 --> 00:06:51,320
How can this be?

101
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,920
Damned monster!

102
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:05,440
Yes. Don't worry about it.

103
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:09,680
His safety is my top priority,
so could you get a car train ready for us?

104
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,820
A direct one.

105
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:12,470
Right.

106
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:15,380
Well, I volunteered to pick him up,

107
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:17,670
so I'll make sure he gets there. See ya!

108
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:27,260
<i>Man, this sucks! I just had my car restored
and it's a total wreck already!</i>

109
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:30,710
<i>33 more loan payments to go,
plus the cost of repairs.</i>

110
00:07:30,710 --> 00:07:33,010
<i>And look! My best dress has been ruined!</i>

111
00:07:33,010 --> 00:07:34,750
Um, Miss Misato...

112
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,380
<i>And I was looking and feeling so nice.</i>

113
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:38,970
Excuse me, Misato?

114
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,550
What?

115
00:07:40,550 --> 00:07:43,350
Are you sure you can just take those?

116
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:46,340
Never mind about that!

117
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:49,650
It's an emergency, and we need
a working car right now, right?

118
00:07:49,650 --> 00:07:53,380
And I'm an international government
official, after all,

119
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,110
so everything's going to be
perfectly fine, okay?

120
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:58,790
I don't think anyone will buy that.

121
00:07:58,790 --> 00:08:03,290
You're no fun. You look cute,
but you're kind of a cold fish.

122
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,460
You think so?

123
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,840
Oh, did I upset you?

124
00:08:08,010 --> 00:08:11,490
Sorry about that! You are a boy, after all.

125
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:14,180
And you're pretty childish for your age.

126
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:23,370
As we predicted, it's regenerating itself.

127
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:27,360
If it couldn't, it wouldn't be
a practical autonomous weapon.

128
00:08:31,310 --> 00:08:34,860
Impressive. It appears it can even upgrade
its own operational functions.

129
00:08:35,290 --> 00:08:37,320
And it seems to have gotten smarter.

130
00:08:38,530 --> 00:08:41,370
It's only a matter of time before
it resumes attacking.

131
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:46,120
The gates are now closing.
Please stand clear.

132
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,030
The special duty organization Nerv?

133
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,420
Now departing.

134
00:08:48,030 --> 00:08:51,660
Yes, it's a secret organization under
the control of the United Nations.

135
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:56,590
This is the C-22 Special Express
departing directly for G33-1.

136
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:53,400
That's where my father is, right?

137
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,400
Well, yeah.

138
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,590
Do you know what he does?

139
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:02,120
This train will bypass all other stations.
Please stand back.

140
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:04,520
My teacher told me his work is vital
for the protection of the human race.

141
00:09:07,430 --> 00:09:10,760
From this point forward, command of this
operation will be entrusted to you.

142
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,560
Show us what you're capable of.

143
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,990
Yes, Sir.

144
00:09:13,990 --> 00:09:20,460
Ikari, we will admit that our weapons
have no effect on the target.

145
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:23,120
But are you sure you can beat this thing?

146
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:25,850
It's what Nerv was created for.

147
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,940
Let's hope you're correct.

148
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,910
The target is still stationary.

149
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:35,420
Our intercept system is currently
7.5% operational.

150
00:09:36,890 --> 00:09:39,200
So, even the UN forces have retired.

151
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,390
What are you going to do?

152
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:43,050
I intend to activate Unit 01.

153
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,640
Unit 01? But we have no pilot.

154
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:50,860
That's not a problem. Another spare
will be delivered soon.

155
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:54,280
Are you taking me to my father?

156
00:09:55,090 --> 00:09:56,950
Yes. Pretty much.

157
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,080
Father...

158
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:07,340
Oh, that's right. Did you get
an ID card from your father?

159
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,550
Yes.

160
00:10:11,990 --> 00:10:12,930
Here it is.

161
00:10:12,930 --> 00:10:13,880
Thanks.

162
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,130
Come.
Gendo Ikari

163
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:18,090
Then read this.

164
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:19,760
Welcome to Nerv

165
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,760
Nerv...

166
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:22,460
My father's agency.

167
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:24,810
Am I going to work for them too?

168
00:10:26,890 --> 00:10:28,590
Of course.

169
00:10:28,590 --> 00:10:33,010
He wouldn't have sent me a letter unless
he needed me for something.

170
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:36,440
I see. So you don't get along with your father.

171
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:39,080
It's the same with me.

172
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,660
Awesome!

173
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,380
It's a real Geo-Front!

174
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:50,220
That's right.

175
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:53,380
This is our secret base.
Nerv Headquarters.

176
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:55,950
This is the key to rebuilding our world.

177
00:10:55,950 --> 00:10:58,540
A fortress for all mankind.

178
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:10,130
That's strange. Isn't this the right way?

179
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:15,360
This is why I hate wearing skirts here.

180
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:18,750
But where the heck did Ritsuko go?

181
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:21,290
I'm sorry. I'm just not used to this place yet.

182
00:11:21,290 --> 00:11:23,230
We passed this spot just a little while ago.

183
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,450
But don't worry about it.

184
00:11:26,450 --> 00:11:29,080
They make these systems
to be used, you know.

185
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:32,050
Would the head of Project E,
Technical Department Division 1,

186
00:11:32,050 --> 00:11:34,920
Dr. Ritsuko Akagi, Dr. Ritsuko Akagi,

187
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:39,680
please contact Captain Misato Katsuragi
of Operations, Division 1, immediately.

188
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:41,310
I don't believe it.

189
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:42,300
She got lost again, didn't she?

190
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,720
Uh, hiya, Ritsuko.

191
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:56,350
What were you doing, Captain Katsuragi?

192
00:11:56,350 --> 00:11:58,360
We're short on both time
and manpower, you know.

193
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,480
Sorry!

194
00:12:03,210 --> 00:12:05,160
So this is the boy?

195
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:09,310
Right. According to the Marduk report,
he's the Third Child.

196
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,100
I'm glad to meet you.

197
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,830
Huh? Sure.

198
00:12:12,830 --> 00:12:17,840
He's just like his father.
Like how he's unendearing.

199
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,440
I'll leave the rest to you.

200
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:26,390
Their first meeting in over three years.

201
00:12:27,190 --> 00:12:31,050
Vice Commander, the target
has started moving again.

202
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:34,230
Right. All personnel, assume
battle stations, Level One.

203
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:38,030
Repeat. All personnel, assume
battle stations, Level One.

204
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:39,540
Prepare for ground-unit interception.

205
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,950
Here we go.

206
00:12:40,950 --> 00:12:42,570
It sounds pretty serious.

207
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:45,470
So, how's Unit 01 doing?

208
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:47,820
It's currently in refrigeration,
using the B-type equipment.

209
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:51,820
Does it really work?
It's never worked before, right?

210
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:57,230
The possibility of activation is 0.000000001%.

211
00:12:57,230 --> 00:12:59,830
We call it, pathetically enough,
the O-9 System.

212
00:12:59,830 --> 00:13:02,540
Does that mean it doesn't work?

213
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:05,120
Oh, don't be insulting. It's not zero.

214
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,950
Well, it's just a number.

215
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:11,560
Anyway, it's a bit too late to be saying,
"Sorry, it didn't work".

216
00:13:20,010 --> 00:13:23,140
Huh? It's completely dark.

217
00:13:26,350 --> 00:13:29,350
A face? A giant robot?

218
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:33,220
You won't find this in the manual.

219
00:13:33,810 --> 00:13:38,080
This is mankind's ultimate
multipurpose decisive weapon,

220
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,500
the synthetic human Evangelion, Unit 01.

221
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:47,030
Built in absolute secrecy,
it is mankind's trump card.

222
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:49,130
Is this part of what my father's been doing?

223
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:50,190
Correct.

224
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,010
It's been a while.

225
00:13:54,510 --> 00:13:55,880
Father...

226
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,820
We're moving out!

227
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:03,680
Moving out?! Unit 00's still in
cryo-stasis, isn't it?

228
00:14:05,170 --> 00:14:08,100
You're not planning to use Unit 01?!

229
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,790
There's no other way.

230
00:14:09,790 --> 00:14:13,030
Hold on! Rei can't do it yet, can she?

231
00:14:13,530 --> 00:14:14,950
We've got no pilot!

232
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:17,080
One's just been delivered.

233
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:19,460
Are you serious?

234
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,490
Shinji Ikari...

235
00:14:21,490 --> 00:14:22,450
Yes?

236
00:14:22,450 --> 00:14:23,630
You will pilot it.

237
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:29,640
But even Rei Ayanami took seven months
to synchronize with her Eva.

238
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:32,350
It's impossible for him to do it!
He just got here!

239
00:14:32,350 --> 00:14:35,210
He just has to sit in the seat.
We don't expect more than that.

240
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:36,240
But...

241
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,730
Repelling that Angel is our ultimate priority.

242
00:14:38,730 --> 00:14:43,020
To do that, we have no choice but to put
aboard the Eva whomever has the chance

243
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,650
to synchronize with it, no matter how slight.

244
00:14:46,570 --> 00:14:49,030
I believe you know that, Captain Katsuragi.

245
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:52,800
I suppose...

246
00:14:53,890 --> 00:14:56,430
Father, why did you send for me?

247
00:14:56,430 --> 00:14:58,620
You know exactly why.

248
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:02,750
So, you're asking me to take this thing
and fight that thing?

249
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:03,920
That's right.

250
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:07,880
No way! Why are you doing this now?!

251
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,530
I thought you didn't need me!

252
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:12,660
I called you because I have a need for you.

253
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,040
Why me?

254
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:19,560
Because no one else can.

255
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,260
No, I can't...

256
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:26,230
I've never even seen anything
like this before! I can't do this!

257
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:28,150
You will be instructed.

258
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:33,080
But there's no way I can do this!

259
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:35,490
I can't pilot it!

260
00:15:37,010 --> 00:15:40,370
If you're going to pilot it, do it now
and quickly. If not, leave!

261
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:54,010
It must have detected our location.

262
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,030
Shinji, we don't have time.

263
00:16:04,810 --> 00:16:05,650
Get into it.

264
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:11,740
No! I didn't come for this! This isn't fair!

265
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:16,490
Shinji, just why did you come here?

266
00:16:18,230 --> 00:16:22,660
You mustn't run! Not from your father,
and most of all not from yourself.

267
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:27,590
I know that! But there's no way I can do it!

268
00:16:35,290 --> 00:16:36,090
Fuyutsuki...

269
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:39,070
Wake up Rei.

270
00:16:39,070 --> 00:16:40,480
Can we use her?

271
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,510
She isn't dead.

272
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:44,660
I understand.

273
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:47,010
Rei.

274
00:16:47,010 --> 00:16:48,050
Yes?

275
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:51,170
Our spare is unusable. You will do it again.

276
00:16:51,170 --> 00:16:51,900
Yes, Sir.

277
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:57,450
Reconfigure Unit 01's system to Rei,
then re-activate!

278
00:16:57,450 --> 00:17:01,190
Roger. Call off the present work,
and begin re-activation.

279
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:07,040
I knew it. I'm not needed after all.

280
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,030
Watch out!

281
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,970
The Eva moved!

282
00:17:52,970 --> 00:17:54,040
What's going on?!

283
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,130
It broke the right arm restraint!

284
00:17:56,130 --> 00:17:58,300
No, that's impossible!

285
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,300
It didn't even have an entry plug inserted!

286
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,640
There's no way it could have moved!

287
00:18:02,850 --> 00:18:05,780
It reacted without any interface?!

288
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:08,100
Or was it protecting...

289
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:08,940
him?

290
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:11,190
We can do it.

291
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:37,010
I mustn't run away. I mustn't run away.
I mustn't run away.

292
00:18:37,010 --> 00:18:38,260
I mustn't run away!

293
00:18:39,730 --> 00:18:41,150
I'll do it.

294
00:18:41,150 --> 00:18:42,180
I'll pilot it!

295
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,250
Cooling process, completed.

296
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,760
Right arm re-secured.

297
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,820
Cage contents now in position for docking.

298
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:51,500
Roger.

299
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,440
Signal terminator plug has been ejected.

300
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:57,530
Roger. Inserting entry plug.

301
00:18:57,530 --> 00:19:01,080
Direct hydro-transmission system,
connection prepared.

302
00:19:04,690 --> 00:19:06,360
Plug fixed in place.

303
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,160
First stage connection initiated.

304
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:15,130
Filling the entry plug.

305
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:17,130
What is this stuff?

306
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:24,360
Don't worry. Once your lungs
are filled with LCL,

307
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:27,000
your blood will be oxygenated directly.

308
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,490
You'll get used to it.

309
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:33,060
I feel nauseous.

310
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:35,310
Stop whining! You're a boy, aren't you?!

311
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:38,050
Connecting main power.

312
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:40,710
All circuits transmitting power.

313
00:19:40,710 --> 00:19:41,520
Roger.

314
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:43,320
Commencing secondary contacts.

315
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:47,180
A-10 nerve connection, normal.

316
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:52,770
Set the thought configuration to Japanese.

317
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:55,740
All preliminary contacts established.
Performance nominal.

318
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:57,630
Bi-directional circuits are open.

319
00:19:57,630 --> 00:20:00,720
Synchronization rate at 41.3%.

320
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,460
Amazing.

321
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:06,410
Harmonics are all normal.
No disturbances identified.

322
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:07,430
We can do it.

323
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,560
Prepare to launch!

324
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,760
Prepare to launch!

325
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,190
Disengage primary lock bolts!

326
00:20:16,730 --> 00:20:20,490
Disengage confirmed.
Disengaging the umbilical bridge.

327
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,650
Disengage secondary lock bolts.

328
00:20:26,070 --> 00:20:28,330
Disengage primary restraints.

329
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:30,410
Likewise, disengage secondary restraints.

330
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:37,080
Release safety locks numbers
one through fifteen.

331
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,460
Release confirmed.

332
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:40,580
Currently, Unit 01's condition is free.

333
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:42,350
Internal batteries fully charged.

334
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:44,380
External battery outlet, normal.

335
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:47,800
Roger. Move Eva Unit 01
to the ejector pad.

336
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:05,200
Launch path is clear. All systems green.

337
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,250
Ready for launch.

338
00:21:07,890 --> 00:21:08,660
Roger.

339
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:11,010
Can we really do this?

340
00:21:11,010 --> 00:21:12,250
Of course.

341
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,500
Unless we defeat the Angels,
we have no future.

342
00:21:16,950 --> 00:21:20,140
Ikari, you're really sure about this?

343
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,460
Launch!

344
00:21:56,490 --> 00:21:58,790
Shinji, don't get killed out there.

345
00:21:58,830 --> 00:22:00,460
TO BE CONTINUED

346
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:06,780
PREVIEW

347
00:23:06,370 --> 00:23:07,930
Eva triumphs over the Angel!

348
00:23:07,930 --> 00:23:10,280
However, that was just the beginning.

349
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:12,220
Shinji runs away from his father.

350
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:15,790
Misato's arrogance leads her
to try to save him.

351
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:18,370
Next Evangelion: "Unfamiliar Ceiling"

352
00:23:18,090 --> 00:23:20,650
I'll give you fan service next time too!

353
00:23:18,830 --> 00:23:21,140
UNFAMILIAR CEILING
